{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Law of Trees: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja74'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 74 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Varuṇavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Warding Tree </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>4. Rukkhadhammajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Law of Trees: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Sādhū sambahulā ñātī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It is well for the many relatives, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>api rukkhā araññajā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the trees born in the forest. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vāto vahati ekaṭṭhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The wind sweeps off one standing alone, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>brahantampi vanappatin”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>even the enormous lord of the forest. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Rukkhadhammajātakaṁ catutthaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
